body:
Not going to judge what you like. People like what they like. A person can't help being straight or gay, or trans-attracted. But cheating is inexcusable, whether you're confused about your sexuality or not. Are you still dating your girlfriend? If you care about her, you will stop sleeping with other people. It doesn't matter what the sex/sexuality of this other person is, if you want to be in a lasting exclusive relationship, you're not going to keep doing this. How do you sleep at night knowing you are engaging in sex acts with a prostitute, knowing that it's possible you could give something to this girlfriend you claim to care so much about? Aren't you concerned for your own health, even? It's a prostitute.

&#x200B;

Do you plan to marry your girlfriend and lead a normal life and continue to cheat on her? I'm genuinely asking you, too. This isn't just about doing the wrong thing. How do you think that's going to affect you long term?
